# Concepts

The model the library implements: here, a moving average over a fixed window.

`MovingAverage<Capacity>` keeps the last `window_samples` samples in a ring of `Capacity` floats and a running
sum. Each `Push()` adds the new sample to the sum and, once the window is full, subtracts the sample it replaces,
so both `Push()` and `Average()` take constant time whatever the window.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    S[Push sample] --> F{window full?}
    F -- no --> A[count + 1]
    F -- yes --> D[sum - oldest]
    A --> W[store, sum + sample]
    D --> W
    W --> M[Average = sum / count]
```

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Memory | `Capacity` floats, a double and a few counters, inside the object |
| Time | O(1) per `Push()` and `Average()` |
| Precision | The sum is a `double`, so long runs of `float` samples do not drift measurably |

